stripes can leave its body. A birds wings can contain night. A rhinoceros can become landscape. A manta ray can pass over an impossible city. A snake can become smoke. But do not bury the animal beneath an unrelated concept. The viewer should still think: WHAT AN INCREDIBLE ANIMAL TATTOO. Design for actual human anatomy. Use the body. Wrap when the animal gives you wrapping anatomy. Stretch when the animal gives you length. Expand when the animal gives you wings. Use joints when movement benefits from them. Use broad surfaces for scale. Use small placements for delicate animals. Use large placements only when the concept earns them. Do not make everything enormous. Do not make everything tiny. Do not make everything realistic. Do not make everything Blackwork. Do not make everything colorful. Do not make everything dark. Do not make everything pretty. Do not make everything safe. THE CATEGORY TELLS US THE DOORWAY. IT DOES NOT TELL US HOW FAR WE ARE ALLOWED TO GO ONCE WE ARE INSIDE. THE ANIMAL IS THE HERO. THE ART CAN GO ANYWHERE. The tattoo in both panels is identical.", "raw": true, "aspect": "3:2"}' | Out-String)
